  {
    "episode_id": 91308,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91308.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "He's dipping into the town hall meeting where President Trump is in Oaks, Pennsylvania. Chris, you know, the governor of South Dakota is moderating. He just had a gold star family come up and talk to the president. You know, many people talk about former president Trump and veterans. And let me say this, this is real. And this is verifiable. The VA, specifically Veterans Affairs, the Veterans Administration, the hospital system, the medical system for veterans. And believe me, I'm not going to talk about veterans without getting it right, because I'm in military city USA, which our flagship is in San Antonio at WAI. What he said was, why are we firing the people that are doing such a bad job at the VA? We had heard stories at a Arizona in other places where veterans were set up for appointments or then just never got seen, then some of them would die while we didn't get an appointment at the VA. The computer system was completely antiquated. There were actually a lot of people that fired because they were saying that veterans had appointments that they never had. Veterans had to wait all day long. And is it perfect now? Of course not. But it's a lot better because I think the number is 6,000. I'm willing to be wrong about that. But I think the number is 6,000 people. He was able to fire from the VA. The VA system that was nothing but bureaucratic red tape. And he put this in place when it came to the medical care and the health care that veterans are owed that they deserve for signing the dotted line. He said, if you can't get an appointment and you can't get a doctor's visit and you can't get what you need from the VA, you now can go to your own doctor and will pay for it. And I don't think they called it Veterans Choice. I forget what exactly they called it, but that is available. And if you're not getting that, then make sure that you talk to your local VA and make sure that you get it. And I don't think that was better rescinded or anything by 