    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "It is representative Greg Lopez. I don't hate the idea, but see, here's the issue. Your ancestors, my ancestors came over legally. They did it the right way. They went through the proper process that was in place whether it be Ellis Island or something else. They did what they were told they had to do to come here legally. The people that are here and they're in the labor force, they must think they're bad people. They're doing jobs that Americans should be doing, and Americans should be doing, and that would raise the wages, because a lot of these people, as you know, are getting paid, you know, a good wage, because they know they can be taken advantage of. I think that it's also benefiting bad employers. So, giving anybody the right to stay, without going through the process that a normal immigrant would go through, is that a magnet or not, do you think?",
