  {
    "episode_id": 91308,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91308.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 92,
    "turn_text": "Look, so what we need to do with this bill, it must, it requires American companies to post for at least six months the posting of a job to allow an American citizen to apply and to get hired. If they can't find someone in six months, then of course then they'll have to sponsor somebody. So these individuals must be sponsored to have a red card. They don't just get a red card because they're hoping to get employment. They already have employment. So the bill is pretty extensive, pretty detailed, but those are the highlights. And my hope is that, look, I'm not going to be there long enough to watch it come in fruition, but my hope is that we start messaging, we start planning the seed, and the 119th Congress will take it up and we'll discuss it. They'll mark up the bill, but it helps us look into the future on how we're going to manage the border.",
