    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91308.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 96,
    "turn_text": "Look, that's all they know about what to do is spend money, right? They want more and more money. Look, America today has a national debt of $35 trillion. And it grows by $1 trillion every hundred days. And so when they want Congress to just arbitrarily give funds again and, you know, increase the budget themselves. They're basically saying we don't care about the American people. We don't care about those hard-working Americans that are paying tax dollars because we want to put more debt on their shoulder. So right now there's no reason for Congress to reconvene because we don't even know the extent of the damage of these hurricanes. And the way it works, you know, remember, I used to be the head of the United States Small Business Administration in Colorado. SBA has a disaster program as well. We work hand in hand with FEMA. You know and you're like seeing SBA screaming and yelling because they know that you know what they have to reassess they have to know what the damage is before they can even ask for money and you know if it makes sense and they're using the money correctly Congress will come together and we'll do some oversight to make sure that you know what Whatever additional dollars we are giving them, it is going to these disaster impacted areas, not to illegal aliens. And that's really the number one thing is that there's a lot of misappropriation going on right now in FEMA.",
